  "term": "double helix",
  "definition": "In this source, a double helix is a dynamic model describing how absorptive capacity and innovation efficiency develop together in a mutually reinforcing, non-linear way. It refers to a synergistic pattern in which their relationship changes with conditions such as policy environment and knowledge spillovers.",
